(a) whether Government is planning to introduce Artificial Intelligence (AI) based education in Government schools;
(b) the number of schools in which AI and Robotics Labs have been established so far;
(c) the number of schools covered under this scheme in the State of Bihar; and
(d) whether there is any proposal to establish at least one AI School of Excellence in each district?

(a) amount of funds approved, released and utilised so far under the Revamped Distribution Sector Scheme (RDSS) in the State of Bihar;
(b) number of smart prepaid meters installed so far under the scheme and the number of new power substations, transmission lines and power distribution infrastructure projects approved and completed thereunder;
(c) the number of projects currently under construction and the timeline for their completion; and
(d) whether the Central Government is considering to approve additional projects under the scheme to ensure uninterrupted and quality power supply in the State of Bihar?

(a) the amount of funds approved and utilised, and the number of new Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise (MSME) units established in the State of Bihar during the last three years under the Prime Minister's Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP), RAMP, CGTMSE, the Micro and Small Enterprises–Cluster Development Programme (MSE-CDP), SFURTI, and other major schemes;
(b) the number of youths, women, and entrepreneurs belonging to the Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes who have benefited through these schemes; and
(c) the extent of direct and indirect employment generated in the State through these schemes?

(a) whether Government is operating any special scheme to promote the production, processing, and marketing of makhana, litchi, maize and other horticultural crops in Bihar;
(b) the number of farmers benefited from the scheme during the last three years;
(c) whether there is any proposal to set up a makhana research and value-addition center in the Darbhanga and Mithilanchal regions; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether any project has been sanctioned during the last three years under the Swadesh Darshan, PRASHAD or any other Central Scheme for the development of the religious, cultural and historical sites in the Mithila region and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government is considering the development of a 'Mithila Tourism Circuit' by connecting Darbhanga, Ahilya Sthan (Kamtaul), Kusheshwar Asthan, Uchaith, Vidyapati Dham and other prominent religious and cultural sites in the Mithila region and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that various projects have been approved in Bihar under the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) and the Rashtriya Gokul Mission (RGM) during the last three years;
(b) if so, the details regarding the year-wise and district-wise approved projects, the funds sanctioned and utilized, and the fish farmers and milk producers benefited therefrom; and
(c) whether Government has formulated any new scheme for the expansion of fish production, dairy infrastructure, cold chain facilities, processing units and breed improvement programmes in Bihar?

(a) whether it is a fact that Bharatmala Project and a number of projects relating to the construction, widening and upgradation of National Highways are currently under implementation in Bihar;
(b) if so, the details of their current status, approved cost, expenditure incurred so far and physical progress in the State, project-wise; and
(c) whether the implementation of any of these projects has been delayed due to land acquisition, forest and environmental clearances or any other reasons and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the project-wise present status of new railway line, doubling, electrification, and station redevelopment projects in Bihar and the number of such projects that are delayed beyond their scheduled timelines;
(b) the details of the funds allocated, released and utilized for these projects during the last five years, year-wise; and
(c) Government's decision regarding the introduction of new Vande Bharat Express, Amrit Bharat and other Express train services for various regions of the State and the commencement of additional rail services in view of the growing passenger demand?

(a) the number of women trained under Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) in Bihar during last five years, district-wise and training sector-wise, details thereof;
(b) the number of women who got employment or self-employment opportunities in Bihar after undergoing training during the said period, district-wise and year-wise, details thereof; and
(c) the details of the employment sectors, trades, salary scales/income brackets and employer institutions for the women trained under the PMKVY in Bihar?

(a) whether Government has developed any mechanism to monitor the functioning of skill development training provider agencies operating in Bihar and Government's assistance being provided to them, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of training institutes inspected under the said mechanism during the last three years and the current year in Bihar; and
(c) the number of training institutes or concerned individuals against whom  action has been taken so far in Bihar for irregularities, financial misconduct or violation of prescribed standards?

(a) the criteria and eligibility conditions prescribed by the Food Corporation of India (FCI) for setting up warehouses in Bihar;
(b) whether Government of Bihar has submitted any proposal or request to the Central Government for setting up new FCI warehouses or expanding existing storage capacity in the State, if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Central Government on the same; and
(c) the number of district-wise FCI-owned and rented warehouses in Bihar currently, along with their total storage capacity?

(a) whether Government has conducted any survey to identify minorities, including the Muslim community, living below the poverty line in the State of Bihar;
(b) if so, the district-wise details of the said survey and the number of beneficiaries identified in Bihar;
(c) the schemes being implemented by the Central Government to improve the economic and social status of minority communities in Bihar; and
(d) the funds allocated, released and spent for Bihar during the last three years and the current year, scheme-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of the rise in adulteration in infant formula, baby milk powder, milk, fruits and vegetables and other essential food items for children, if so, the details of the cases reported in the country particularly in the State of Bihar over the past three years;
(b) whether specific standards have been set to ensure the quality of food products intended for children; and
(c) the strict punitive and monitoring measures taken by Government to prevent the manufacture and sale of adulterated food items to safeguard children’s health?

(a) the number of beneficiaries registered and the number of hospitals empanelled under the Central Government Health Scheme (CGHS) currently across the country, particularly in the State of Bihar;
(b) whether it has come to the notice of Government that the availability of cashless treatment under CGHS in the State of Bihar is limited, as compared to various other States of the country, if so, the steps taken to strengthen the same; and
(c) whether after revision of CGHS package rates, beneficiaries across the country and in the State of Bihar are required to make additional payments at hospitals?

(a) the details of Central schemes currently being implemented for conservation and promotion of Mithila paintings, Tikuli and Manjusha art;
(b) the number of artists in Bihar who have been provided training or financial assistance under the schemes; and
(c) the specific steps taken by Government for promotion of these traditional folk arts at the national and international levels?

(a) the Central schemes currently being implemented in the State of Bihar to provide relief to farmers affected by floods and droughts;
(b) the number of farmers affected by floods and drought in Bihar that have been given compensation over the past three years; and
(c) the steps being taken by Government to make the relief and compensation distribution process more effective and timebound?

(a) whether Government proposes to set up another Ayurvedic Research Centre in the State of Bihar to promote Ayurveda;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of Ayurvedic Research Centres functioning in the country including Bihar, State-wise; and
(d) the details of funds allocated and utilized for Research and Development in the said Centres during the last three years and the current year?

(a) whether Government has carried out a review of the progress of health services under the Ayushman Bharat–Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY), National Health Mission (NHM), Maternal and Child Health Program, and immunization schemes in the State of Bihar, if so, the details of approved, completed and pending projects, district-wise;
(b) the amount of central assistance allocated, released and spent in the State of Bihar under the above-mentioned schemes during the last three years and the current year; and
(c) the future plans to address maternal mortality, infant mortality, malnutrition, communicable diseases and emerging health challenges in a densely populated State of Bihar?

(a) whether Ministry is aware that income-based tuition fee waivers and financial aid schemes are available to economically disadvantaged students in centrally funded technical institutions such as IITs and NITs;
(b) reasons why such income-based waivers or financial aid mechanisms are currently unavailable to students enrolled in the Indian Institutes of Science Education and Research (IISERs);
(c) reasons for this disparity in policy among centrally funded institutions of national importance; and
(d) whether Ministry proposes to take steps to ensure parity in financial aid provisions, including the extension of income-based fee waivers to students of IISERs?

(a) whether Government has formulated any policy to continue the existing temporary cinema halls in Delhi on a permanent basis by changing the land use through an Extraordinary Gazette notification in the year 2013, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of temporary cinema halls allowed to continue on a permanent basis so far through change in land use; and
(c) whether any new conditions have been added after the notification was issued through the Extraordinary Gazette, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the manner in which the Ministry is ensuring that two lakh micro-enterprises benefit from the credit-linked component of the Pradhan Mantri Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) scheme and the average loan sanction time after Detailed Project Report (DPR) approval;
(b) the new provisions implemented to increase the participation of women and SC/ST entrepreneurs under the PMFME scheme after August 2025 and the manner in which the Ministry is evaluating the impact of higher subsidies for these groups; and
(c) whether the guidelines related to enhanced financing for Common Service Providers under PMFME have been finalized?

(a) present status of implementation of Industrial Park Rating System (IPRS) 3.0, including number of industrial parks assessed so far and States/UTs participating in the exercise;
(b) details of criteria and methodology adopted under IPRS 3.0 to benchmark industrial parks across parameters such as sustainability, logistics connectivity, digitalization, infrastructure quality, and tenant feedback;
(c) details of steps being taken to support underperforming industrial parks and States/UTs in addressing deficiencies identified;
(d) whether Government proposes to integrate IPRS 3.0 with other national platforms such as PM Gati Shakti, NICDC’s industrial corridor systems, or Unified Logistics Interface Platform (ULIP) to enhance data interoperability; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a fresh exercise since 2024 to identify obsolete or redundant Central Acts for repeal and if so, the number of such Acts identified;
(b) whether the 23rd Law Commission has submitted any interim recommendations on revising, simplifying or repealing outdated Central laws;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government has set targets to further reduce compliance burden through amendment, consolidation or repeal of laws;
(e) if so, the action plan and timeline thereof;
(f) the steps being taken to simplify the drafting style of Central legislation for greater public accessibility; and
(g) the training or capacity-building initiatives which have been undertaken?

(a) the manner in which the draft PPA Bill seeks to protect job seekers from fraudulent and unethical recruitment practices;
(b) the manner in which mandatory registration and an integrated career service portal would strengthen oversight of private placement agencies;
(c) whether stakeholder consultations were undertaken on the draft PPA Bill;
(d) the manner in which the Bill enables better coordination between Government bodies and private agencies;
(e) the grievance-redressal mechanisms provided for job seekers;
(f) its expected impact on India’s global employment competitiveness; and
(g) the manner in which penal provisions would deter malpractices and ensure ethical conduct?

(a) the manner in which the Ministry is ensuring that simplified CRZ clearance procedures for Blue Economy projects do not harm ecologically sensitive areas such as mangroves and coral reefs;
(b) the measures being taken to strengthen State Coastal Zone Management Authorities (SCZMAs) for rigorous, independent monitoring and enforcement of CRZ norms; and
(c) whether the Ministry has finalised guidelines for implementing the National Marine Litter Policy and the manner in which it is working with coastal States to manage plastic waste from fishing and tourism?

(a) the manner in which the staffing and technical gaps in ASI’s excavation branches are addressed;
(b) the manner in which  the timely completion of reports at 22 sites with ? 15 crore budget for 2025-26 would be ensured;
(c) the steps taken to implement a transparent, single-window clearance system for academic and foreign archaeological collaborations;
(d) manner in which LiDAR, GIS and drones are being used to digitally map the heritage sites and the timeline for completion of national digital map; and
(e) manner in which the conservation of ancient religious monuments with enforcement against encroachment is being balanced?

(a) the crop varieties developed during the last five years using radiation techniques;
(b) the features or characteristics of newly introduced crop varieties that distinguish them from the earlier ones;
(c) whether any assessment or examination has been undertaken regarding the safety of these new varieties for consumption;
(d) if so, the details of studies or evaluations conducted in this regard; and
(e) whether these crop varieties have been released after field trials for cultivation by farmers and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the year-wise number of beneficiaries under the Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana (PMMVY) and whether this scheme has increased the institutional delivery rate among pregnant women;
(b) the improvements marked in the transparency and efficiency of benefit distribution due to the adoption of digital platforms and Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) system in the implementation of the PMMVY; and
(c) whether there has been a significant improvement in nutrition awareness and antenatal check-ups (ANC Check-ups) in mothers as a result of the financial assistance and counselling services provided under the PMMVY if so, the  details thereof?

(a) the latest progress achieved under the eTransport Mission Mode Project, including the current number of vehicle registrations, driving licences issued, challans processed, PUCC certificates generated, digitized driving schools and other key service metrics till date;
(b) whether the Ministry has undertaken any assessment of the impact of contactless and online citizen services under Vahan, Sarathi, eChallan, NextGen mParivahan and related applications, particularly in reducing RTO footfalls, service delivery time and instances of manual intervention; and
(c) whether the Ministry has reviewed performance of systems such as PUCC centres, Automated Testing Stations (ATS) and Accredited Driving Testing Centres?

(a) the financial assistance that has been given so far to the sportspersons of Bihar performed at the national and international level;
(b) whether the talented sportspersons of Bihar are being given coaching, diet and other facilities free of cost by Government; and 
(c) whether Government is contemplating to establish a sports university in Bihar?

(a) the number of colleges and universities of Bihar where National Service Scheme (NSS) units are being run and whether Government is considering to increase the same;
(b) the schemes that have been run so far by  Nehru Yuva Kendra Sangathan (NYKS) to provide employment oriented training to the youth of Bihar; and 
(c) whether any annual plan for Youth Leadership Training camps has been set in Bihar under Nehru Yuva Kendra Sangathan?

(a) the details of the Pradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Anna Yojana (PM-GKAY);
(b) the objectives of this scheme;
(c) the number of  beneficiaries/families that are currently covered under this scheme; and
(d) the quantity of foodgrains distributed by the States/UTs in the current year?

