(a) the challenges addressed by the Ministry through the Jan Poshan Kendra pilot project;
(b) the States where this modernisation pilot study has been undertaken and the number of Fair Price Shops(FPS) included in it, the details thereof; and
(c) the timeline and targets for completion of this modernization process?

(a) whether Government has considered partnerships to enhance linguistic and cultural diversity on the Waves Over-The-Top (OTT) platform; 
(b) the strategies which Waves OTT is adopting to compete with private OTT platforms; and
(c) the promotional efforts being made to make Waves OTT popular and accessible to the public in rural areas and Tier II/III towns?

(a) whether Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) is the world's largest crop insurance scheme;
(b) if so, the details of the major initiatives taken by Government to make this possible and increase  the number of farmers covered under the scheme as a result of these initiatives;
(c) the details of the total amount of premium paid by farmers since 2022, the number of farmers who received compensation during this period and the total amount distributed to them;
(d) whether any major improvements have been made in the scheme as compared to the earlier crop insurance schemes; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether credit assistance has been provided by Government for setting up cold storage under Mission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH);
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has assessed the demand and availability of cold storage facilities for fruits and vegetables; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) whether Department of Atomic Energy, through its grant-in-aid institution, Tata Memorial Centre, has collaborated with Wipro GE Healthcare to promote cancer research and innovation in India;
(b) whether this collaboration involves development and implementation of Artificial Intelligence (AI) based applications for medical imaging, clinical workflow and advanced visualization tools in the field of oncology; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken any steps towards implementing the Joint Declaration approved  at the 10th BRICS Culture Ministers' Meeting; 
(b) the countries with which bilateral agreements have been signed following discussions during this meeting; 
(c) whether the Ministry has prepared any action plan to integrate traditional knowledge systems into climate adaptation strategies as discussed in the meeting; and
(d) if so, the major steps being taken to achieve these objectives?

(a) the initiatives being implemented under the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana(PMMSY)to enhance fisheries infrastructure in Tripura, Bihar and Maharashtra;
(b) the manner in which Government is working to improve employment opportunities in the fisheries sector in Tripura, Bihar and Maharashtra;
(c) the plan to expand organic fish clusters on the lines of Tripura, Bihar and Maharashtra; and
(d) the manner in which Government is supporting fisheries cooperatives and startups in Tripura, Bihar and Maharashtra under PMMSY?

(a) whether there is any proposal to open a Central University in the districts falling under the Mithila region of Bihar;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) if not, whether any scheme has been implemented regarding Universities and higher education; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of schools upgraded and the newly constructed residential schools/hostels under the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA);
(b) whether this scheme covers Information Communication Technology (ICT) and digital initiatives such as smart schools and smart classrooms;
(c) if so, total number of such schools; and
(d) major interventions proposed at all levels of school education under the scheme?

(a) whether Government has details of companies that spend their mandatory Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) funds on services such as education and health, if so, the total amount of CSR funds spent on health and education;
(b) if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government intends to introduce a system that would institutionalize the use of CSR funds by companies; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the steps being taken to ensure coordination between the States and the Central law enforcement agencies through the "BHARATPOL" portal;
(b) whether there is any mechanism to track and evaluate the effectiveness of the "BHARATPOL" portal to improve the  international police cooperation;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the  initiatives being taken so that district and local level law enforcement agencies can use the "BHARATPOL" portal effectively?

(a) the total length of National Highways (NH) constructed by Government during the last five years;
(b) the total length of National High-Speed Corridors constructed by Government during the last five years, the details thereof, State-wise; and 
(c) the total length of four lane or wider National Highways (excluding high-speed corridors) constructed by Government during the last five year, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) the measures being taken to ensure the financial assistance provided under Government schemes reaches the small and marginal fish farmers effectively;
(b) the impact of subsidies provided under schemes such as Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMSSY) and Fisheries and Aquaculture Infrastructure Development Fund (FIDF) on the income and production levels of fish farmers in the last five years; and 
(c) whether any new policies are being formulated to enhance the global competitiveness of the country's fisheries sector, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Indian Universities would be encouraged to establish academic partnerships and research collaborations with the University of Southampton; 
(b) whether Government is planning to ease regulations for the establishment of more Foreign University campuses in the country;   
(c) if so, the details thereof and the steps being taken regarding this; and  
(d) the measures proposed to be taken to ensure inclusivity so that students from diverse socio-economic backgrounds can also be benefitted from the said initiative?

(a) the steps being taken to enable students from rural and economically weaker backgrounds to avail internship opportunities under the said scheme;  
(b) whether there is any provision to increase the number of internship seats on the basis of demand basis especially for students belonging to agriculture and rural development sector;  
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether there has been any partnership between the Sahakar Mitra Internship Scheme and other major Government initiatives such as Startup India, Aatmanirbhar Bharat or Digital India to strengthen the cooperative sector; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the targets set for wheat procurement for Rabi Marketing Season (RMS) 2025-26, State-wise including Rajasthan and the actual procurement achieved, so far;
(b) the average time taken for MSP payments to reach farmers and steps being taken to ensure timely disbursement in RMS 2025-26; and
(c) whether Government has set up a real-time monitoring mechanism to track wheat procurement, payments and stock quality, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the manner in which Training Programme in Chemical and Petrochemical Industrial Safety helps Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) in the chemical and petrochemical sector improve their safety standards;
(b)  whether any new policy intiatives are being introduced based on the outcomes of this training programme; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the plans of Government to bridge the gap between traditional Ayurveda and modern systems of medicine using the findings from the initiative i.e. "Desh Ka Prakriti Parikshan Abhiyan";
(b) whether there is any plan to integrate this Abhiyan with mainstream healthcare services such as Ayushman Bharat or other public health programmes;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Ministry has any roadmap for the second phase of "Desh Ka Prakriti Parikshan Abhiyan"; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the specific mechanisms that are proposed to be put in place to ensure that Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) can effectively scale up to meet the revised investment and turnover limits;
(b) the steps proposed to be taken to ensure that banks and financial institutions actually extend the enhanced credit guarantee cover to eligible MSMEs and startups;
(c) the safeguards that are in place to prevent misuse of credit schemes or fraudulent loan applications; and
(d) whether there will be any special provisions for rural and women-led micro enterprises to access these credit cards easily?

(a) whether Government has conducted a feasibility study for interlinking of Krishna-Cauvery and Pennar-Palar river basins;
(b) the steps the Central Government has taken so far to ensure the flow of surplus water from the proposed Mahanadi-Godavari basin to the Krishna-Cauvery and Pennar-Palar basins; and
(c) the present status of the Central funding for the Upper Bhadra Project and by when the grant is likely to be released to the State of Karnataka?

(a) whether Government has prepared any detailed strategy to ensure uninterrupted supply of 906 million tonnes of coal for the power sector in financial year 2025-26;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the specific measures  taken to address the expected coal shortage during peak summer months; and
(d) whether any contingency plan exists for unexpected demand surge?

