(a) whether Government has conducted any impact assessment on the transition from physical pilot licenses to Electronic Personnel License (EPL), if so, the details thereof;
(b) the specific measures taken to ensure the security and authenticity of digital pilot licenses and prevent their potential misuse or fraud; and
(c) whether Government has received any feedback from airlines, pilot associations, or international regulatory bodies regarding the implementation of EPL, if so, the actions that are being taken in response thereto?

(a) whether the policy framed by Government for continuation of existing temporary cinema halls in Delhi on permanent basis by changing the land use through an Extraordinary Gazette Notification in 2013 has subsequently been added some more conditions, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether the subsequent conditions are applicable uniformly for all plot sizes belonging to cinema hall owners; and
(c) the number of landowners who have so far conducted traffic impact study as per the condition and submitted its report to Government?

(a) whether Government has formulated any policy to continue the existing temporary cinema halls in Delhi on a permanent basis by changing the policy in regard to land use through an Extraordinary Gazette Notification in the year 2013, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of temporary cinema halls that have been allowed to continue on a permanent basis so far through the change in policy regarding land use; and
(c) whether new conditions have been added after issuing the notification through Extraordinary Gazette, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether it is a fact that Bihar produces 85 per cent of the total production of fox nut (makhana) in the country, and whether the Ministry has any special plan to promote this industry;
(b) whether there is any provision to provide financial assistance for conducting training programmes for farming, processing and marketing to improve fox nut industry; and
(c) whether any loan facility is available to the farmers engaged in small industries ancillary to the fox nut industry?

(a) whether any place has been designated for promoting sports in Darbhanga or any nearby district in the State of Bihar;
(b) whether there is any plan to promote various sports in a State like Bihar through any scheme under the Ministry;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the manner in which the Ministry plans to provide better sports facilities in Bihar?

P

(a) whether there is any plan to establish National Institute of Naturopathy in the State of Bihar just as it is being run in Pune, Maharashtra;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, whether any special scheme can be formulated to operate it in the State of Bihar?

(a) the efforts made so far to strengthen the cooperative sector after the formation of a separate Ministry of Cooperation;
(b) the steps taken to ensure that the efforts made, reach the grassroots level as most of the farmers and villagers are associated with  the cooperative sector; and
(c) the details of efforts made in this regard?

(a) whether Government is aware of the news reports that all the seats in all the trains going to Bihar during the most popular festival of Bihar i.e. 'Chhath' have been booked in just one hour of opening of reservations four months in advance;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to conduct any inquiry in view of the possibility of any mismanagement in this regard; and 
(d) the details of special plan being considered by Government to facilitate passengers intending to visit Bihar on the eve of 'Chhath' festival?

(a)  the reasons for not yet operating any Makhana based industry by Government in Darbhanga district of Bihar despite the district is a major area of Makhana production; 
(b)  Government's  plans to set up Makhana based industries on a large scale in Darbhanga district in view of the immense possibilities, the details thereof;
(c)  the details of scheme of Government to train local youth for manufacturing biscuits, chips and other nutritious food items etc. using Makhana as raw-material; and 
(d)  timeframe by when all the schemes are likely to be started?

(a) whether it is a fact that no new superfast train for long distances has been introduced for the last several years from Darbhanga, the railway station that provides maximum revenue for Samastipur Division;
(b) the number of proposals for new train operations from Darbhanga railway station pending with the Railway Board;
(c) whether the Ministry has any proposal to introduce Vande Bharat trains from Darbhanga to New Delhi and Darbhanga to Patna; and
(d) if so, the details regarding the operation of the said Vande Bharat trains?
